@*image tags, src = source, alt = alternative text, if image doesnt load this is displayed instead, also good for accessibility, search engine optimisated etc
    Can store images in wwwroot folder or you can link to an external image
*@
<img src="https://i.pinimg.com/originals/69/fe/fa/69fefa832971fe6bd318226aea9557b6.gif" alt="huh cat">

@*Post tells us how the data will be sent to the server*@
<form method = "post">

    @*The type of data we want submitted from the form*@
    <label>Username: </label> @*Prompt for user*@
    <input type="text">

    <label>Password: </label> @*Prompt for user*@
    <input type="password">

    <label>Subscribe to newsletter? </label> @*Prompt for user*@
    <input type="checkbox">

    <label>Date of birth </label> @*Prompt for user*@
    <input type="date">

    @*When this button is clicked submit all of the data to the server*@
    <button type = "submit">Submit</button>
</form>

<div label>
    <form method = "post">
        <div>
            <label for="username">Username: </label> @*id in the input matches it to this label*@
            <input type="text" id="username" name="Username" required /> @*required is needed to avoid an error if a user doesnt submit an answer and the form gets an null answer*@
        </div>
        <div>
            <label for="newsletter">Subscribe to our newsletter?  </label> @*id in the input matches it to this label*@
            <input type="checkbox" id="newsletter" name="Newsletter" required/> 
        </div>
        <div>
            <button type = "submit">Submit</button>
        </div>
    </form>
</div>

@*Checks if the form has been submitted, found in the .cshtml.cs file, runs the below code if true

Links together the cshtml form data submission with the cshtml.cs class that binds the data - then things can be done with the data*@
@if (Model.Submitted == true) 
{
    <div>
        <h2>Form Submission Result<h2/>
        <p>Username: @Model.Username</p>

        <p>Newsletter Subscription:
            @if (Model.Newsletter == true)
            {
                <span>Subscribed</span>
            }
            else 
            {
                <span>Not Subscribed</span>
            }
        </p>
    </div>
}